60,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Looking at the options, Meridian Systems seems the most sustainable. Its fixed configuration and regional support team provide the simplicity and clear ownership we need to protect our stretched staff and avoid training failures.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"I'm with Misaki! Meridian Systems sounds great because it's a hosted suite, which might be easier on our old yard devices. Plus, a regional team means we have real people to help us!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Meridian Systems is the only logical choice. Its hosted suite suggests a bundled approach, avoiding the fragmented, escalating costs of modular systems like Corvus, which my research shows are a long-term financial drain.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"I agree with everyone! Meridian Systems sounds wonderful because the regional service team means we'll have someone to turn to if things break, so nobody has to feel lost or stressed!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,The logic is quite compelling. Meridian avoids the fragmented licensing of Corvus and the risk of external migration errors seen with Tessera. A fixed configuration is a prudent shield against the scope creep that has plagued us.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"I agree. A fixed configuration is essential because it prevents the system from becoming overly complex, which would only overwhelm our remaining administrators and lead the depot crews to abandon the tool.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"Exactly! If it's a fixed configuration, it's less likely to be some fancy thing that doesn't work on our old scanners. We need something that just works without needing a million tweaks!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Kenji, simplicity is a financial safeguard as well. A fixed configuration typically implies a more predictable cost structure, whereas the ""configurable workflows"" of Tessera often hide a trail of expensive professional service fees.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, that's so true! And since it's a hosted suite, we won't have to worry about those scary upgrade windows that we keep skipping. It'll stay current without making everyone feel overwhelmed!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, a most astute observation. By shifting the burden of maintenance to the host, we avoid the tragedy of a system that quietly ages into obsolescence while we wait for a testing window that never arrives.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"I agree. By reducing the technical burden on our internal team, we can better manage the loss of our experienced administrators and ensure the transition doesn't break the people holding us together.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I'm totally on board! Meridian is the safest bet for the yard. It's way better than Anchor's on-site servers or Corvus's messy modules. Let's pick the one that actually works for everyone!,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"I concur. Meridian Systems provides the most transparent financial path. By avoiding the modular licensing of Corvus and the marketplace model of Tessera, we eliminate the risk of the hidden, climbing costs that plague our budget.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Yumi,,I'm so happy we all agree! Meridian Systems feels like the kindest choice for our team because it gives us a clear partner to rely on and a system that stays fresh. I vote for Meridian Systems!,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,It is a rare and beautiful thing to find such complete alignment. Meridian Systems offers a sanctuary from both the financial fragmentation of Corvus and the operational volatility of Tessera. I vote for Meridian Systems.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Misaki,,I agree. Meridian Systems is the only choice that respects our current staffing limitations and ensures the burden of the transition doesn't fall on an already exhausted team. I vote for Meridian Systems.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Kenji,,I'm totally in! Meridian is the best way to make sure the yard doesn't crash and the people on the floor aren't left hanging. I vote for Meridian Systems!,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"The evidence is conclusive. Meridian Systems avoids the modular licensing traps of Corvus and the hidden costs of Tessera's marketplace, ensuring our long-term budget remains stable. I vote for Meridian Systems.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Yumi,,I'm just so glad we could all find a solution that makes everyone feel safe and supported! I'm casting my final vote for Meridian Systems!,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I find the logic inescapable. To choose otherwise would be to invite the very systemic frictions we have spent this session identifying. I cast my final vote for Meridian Systems.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
